[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read by cause instead of by subject, it holds three
problems. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket, so the parser fix does not close the other two.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Day-first tenants (every tenant on
file) get day and month swapped: a 7 April booking goes out on 4 July. This is the bug #4471
describes, and the fix that is queued.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells day-first people to type month first.** Its date field shows
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people type what it says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. The swap
looks the same as `parser`, but the cause is the form's hint, so the parser fix does not touch it.
Only form reports from tenants on booking-v3 have it. Intake tags it from the reporter's browser,
which is often wrong; the table counts by tenant and channel ([causes.ts](/kb/triage/dedupe)).

**`one-day-move`: the date moves by one day, not a swap.** "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says
Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." "Every booking in June
is one day off."
Nothing is swapped, so neither fix covers it. The pattern points at time zones or the change to
summer time. #4471's table files these under `parser` by tenant and keeps them in a footnote, so no
ticket ever tracked them.

## How this was counted

- Every report merged into #4471, once per report id.
- `parser` and `hint`: tenant locale and booking form from the tenant directory, plus the channel
  the report came in by (`causes.ts`). Not the intake tag.
- `one-day-move`: the reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), checked against
  their bodies.
- Every number on this page is computed at render time from the export in `src/lib/data`.

